:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∣20\\,∣\\,=20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of a number gives the distance between the number and zero on a number line.\n\n![](images/47/479a1bd306e54770c7fd87759942bdbae9dbd656a74f81a8fe628b9ca3a2a089.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441511 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441503 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441511 #edb/ref 1069 "q-136475" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441511 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441511 #edb/ref 1071 "$|-\\frac{29}{4}|=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441511 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "36a54bb6-398d-5b72-b8d0-6330c32d47d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441511 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the absolute value of $-\\frac{29}{4},$ we simply drop the negative sign:\n\n$$\n|-\\frac{29}{4}|=\\frac{29}{4}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of a number gives the distance between the number and zero on a number line.\n\n![](images/4b/4b14d3a97ab19147b8479dc507072fed299c84e26a0f2911476c79cdc6984bc6.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441512 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441512 #edb/ref 1069 "q-69921" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441512 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441512 #edb/ref 1071 "$∣-25\\,∣=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441512 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5945d93c-a70a-521a-869b-73c5d038b545" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441512 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the absolute value of $-25,$ we simply drop the negative sign:\n\n$$\n∣-25\\,∣=25\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of a number gives the distance between the number and zero on a number line.\n\n![](images/b2/b2cbf17501c131978f3f15c491a6a34d2d400f1c8d325578c07e12a1aa1a8a00.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441513 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441513 #edb/ref 1069 "q-185403" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441513 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441513 #edb/ref 1071 "$∣18\\,∣\\,=\\,${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441513 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6b401926-c0e5-5474-b55e-50619c2b3ed1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441513 #edb/ref 1074 "The absolute value of a positive number equals the number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∣18\\,∣\\,=18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of a number gives the distance between the number and zero on a number line.\n\n![](images/a5/a537db0a91825ac6d74dca4222544613e97d48ee7bd64ea61b9e19dc7b314450.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441514 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441514 #edb/ref 1069 "q-136500" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441514 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441514 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/72/722ca4cfa2c3eaf0afb887412e727341c18c2419a8d3ae43a2c6a36fe7e864d7.png)\n\nThe point shown above represents a number on a number line. The absolute value of this number is $\\frac{19}{6}.$ What is the number?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441514 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9184b1c1-18a5-54d0-ad44-5eac57556d33" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441514 #edb/ref 1074 "The number is *negative* because it is to the *left* of zero.\n\nThe absolute value of the number is $\\frac{19}{6},$ so the distance between that number and zero on a number line is $\\frac{19}{6}.$ \n\nThe negative number at a distance of $\\frac{19}{6}$ from zero is $-\\frac{19}{6}.$\n\n![](images/9a/9a78acce2ae81830a505b53a9b5ea2d44c113fc49f733e86a2e064f5683f3f9b.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441515 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441515 #edb/ref 1069 "q-136480" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441515 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441515 #edb/ref 1071 "$|-\\frac{13}{4}\\,|=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441515 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "92383c72-78eb-58ae-9945-4a084c79c027" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441515 #edb/ref 1074 